{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310693,"nonce":"eS+2eWIdR9y4ZZLqncbRP0hUVUA=","title":"FIXED — `is` operator + Std.isOfType walked broken when extends chain used canonicalised TypeIds. Two parts: is_subclass_of needs SymbolId ...","message":"`test_rtti` was silently failing 3/14 assertions despite PASS exit code:\n- `var d:Animal = new Dog(...); d is Dog` → false (expected true)\n- `var c = new Cat(...); c is Animal` → false (expected true)\n- `Std.isOfType(d, Dog)` → false (expected true)\n\n\nTwo independent issues in [hir_to_mir.rs](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs):\n\n\n`HirClass.extends` is set in [tast_to_hir.rs:603-611](compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs#L603-L611) to `TypeId::from_raw(parent_sym.as_raw())` — a synthetic TypeId derived from the parent's SymbolId for cross-context stability. `type_table.get(synthetic_type_id)` returns None.\n\n`is_subclass_of` at [hir_to_mir.rs:32790-32796](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L32790) walked the extends chain and bailed when `type_table.get(parent_type_id)` returned None. Result: every parent lookup failed silently → both upcast (`Cat is Animal`) and downcast (`(d:Animal) is Dog`) reported false.\n\n\n[hir_to_mir.rs:19269](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L19269) (pre-fix) used `tgt_sym.as_raw() as i64` as the target type_id when calling `haxe_object_is_instance`. The runtime registry is keyed by MIR `typedef.type_id` (= `runtime_type_id(target) - 1000`), not the bare SymbolId — so even when `is_subclass_of` correctly identified a downcast, the runtime walk never matched the registry entry.\n\n\n1. `is_subclass_of` — when `type_table` lookup of `parent_type_id` returns None, fall back to `SymbolId::from_raw(parent_type_id.as_raw())` and consult the symbol table. Same pattern already used in `register_class_metadata` (for `class_parent_map.insert`) and `lower_constructor_body` (for parent ctor lookup).\n\n2. Class-downcast TypeCheck branch — compute `target_type_id` as `runtime_type_id(*expected) - 1000` (matching what `register_class_from_mir` stores), instead of `tgt_sym.as_raw()`. The `Std.isOfType` runtime path was also fixed by the same change, because the compile-time evaluation now short-circuits correctly for `Animal/Dog`-style hierarchies.\n\n\nAny time you add an `extends`-chain walk in `hir_to_mir.rs`, remember `HirClass.extends` can be either a real TypeId (resolvable via `type_table`) OR a `TypeId::from_raw(symbol_id.as_raw())` canonical form. Always provide the SymbolId fallback. Also: any runtime call comparing object-header type_ids must use `runtime_type_id - 1000`, never bare `SymbolId.as_raw()`.\n\nVerification: full suite 128/128 in `./run_haxe_tests.sh` after fix; `test_rtti` now prints all 14 expected values.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_rtti_inheritance_walk` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}